.\" Manual page for slotbook, the IITM Explainable Slotbook CLI (v3).
.\" View with:  man ./man/slotbook.1
.TH SLOTBOOK 1 "November 2026" "slotbook 3.0" "IITM Explainable Slotbook"
.SH NAME
slotbook \- generate and explain an IITM course slotbook, with advisory prerequisite warnings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slotbook
.B \-\-input
.I DIR
.RB [ \-\-output
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-solver
.BR unitime | cpsat ]
.RB [ \-\-time\-limit
.IR SECONDS ]
.br
.RB [ \-\-prerequisites
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-completed\-courses
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-prerequisite\-check ]
.PP
.B slotbook \-\-help
.PP
From the repository, run it through Maven:
.PP
.RS
.B mvn exec:java \-Dexec.args="\-\-input data/feasible \-\-output output/demo"
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slotbook
reads course, slot, conflict and preference CSV files, assigns one lecture slot to every
course and explains each assignment.
.PP
Hard rules always hold: one slot per course from its allowed set (or its fixed slot), no
lecture over the course's own lab, no overlap between protected course pairs, no instructor
teaching two overlapping meetings, and no two lectures in the same room at once.
Overlaps are computed from real weekly meeting times, not slot letters.
.PP
Within those rules the solver minimises three costs: instructor slot penalties (1 when an
instructor gave no preference for a slot), 2 for moving a course away from its historical
slot, and student clashes (pair weight \(mu overlapping meetings \(mu 3).
.PP
The default solver is UniTime's course timetabling engine
.RB ( cpsolver ),
a local\-search heuristic that keeps improving until the time limit. The
.B cpsat
solver is the exact OR\-Tools model from v1 and can prove optimality on small inputs.
.PP
Explanations are deterministic and identical for both solvers: for the chosen slot they list
the rules satisfied and the penalties paid; for every other slot they say why it was
rejected or give its estimated cost. No language model is involved.
.SS Prerequisite warnings (new in v3)
If prerequisite rules are supplied, each student's ranked courses are checked against the
courses they have completed. A ranked course whose prerequisite is not completed produces a
warning.
.PP
Warnings are
.BR advisory :
they are printed and exported, but they never block solving, never change the exit status,
and are never passed to the solver. The slotbook is the same with or without them.
.PP
Grades
.BR U ,
.B W
and
.B I
do not count as completed; every other grade (S, A\(enE, P) does. A retaken course counts if
any attempt completed it. A student with no completion rows at all gets a single
.B NO_COMPLETION_RECORD
warning rather than one warning per prerequisite.
.PP
The preference portal produces both files: professors declare prerequisites, and students
upload their grade card, which the portal parses into
.IR completed_courses.csv .
Student\-uploaded grade cards are not verified.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-input " DIR"
Required. Directory containing the five solver inputs listed under
.BR FILES .
It may also hold the two optional prerequisite files.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " DIR"
Where to write the results (default:
.IR output ).
Created if missing.
.TP
.BR \-\-solver " " unitime | cpsat
.B unitime
(default) runs UniTime cpsolver;
.B cpsat
runs the v1 OR\-Tools CP\-SAT model.
.TP
.BI \-\-time\-limit " SECONDS"
Positive search time limit (default 10). UniTime always uses the whole limit; CP\-SAT stops
early once it proves optimality.
.TP
.BI \-\-prerequisites " FILE"
Prerequisite rules, overriding
.IR DIR /prerequisites.csv.
The file must exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-completed\-courses " FILE"
Completed courses, overriding
.IR DIR /completed_courses.csv.
The file must exist.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-prerequisite\-check
Skip prerequisite warnings even when the files are present. Nothing about the solve changes.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit without solving.
.PP
Unknown options are an error (exit status 2). In v2 they were silently ignored.
.SH FILES
.SS Required inputs (in DIR)
.TP
.I courses.csv
course_id, title, semester_group, course_type, instructor, class_size, historical_slot,
fixed_slot, allowed_slots (pipe\-separated), additional_slot, room
.TP
.I slots.csv
slot_id, days, start_times, lengths, category (LECTURE or LAB)
.TP
.I hard_conflicts.csv
course_1, course_2, reason
.TP
.I instructor_preferences.csv
instructor, slot, penalty (0 or more), reason
.TP
.I student_preferences.csv
student_id, course_id, rank
.SS Optional inputs (v3)
.TP
.I prerequisites.csv
course_id, prereq_course_id
.TP
.I completed_courses.csv
student_id, course_id, grade, and optionally term and source
.RB ( grade_card
by default;
.B admin
is reserved for academic\-section records)
.SS Outputs (in the output directory)
.TP
.I generated_slotbook.csv
One row per course with its assigned slot.
.TP
.I assignment_explanations.csv
Reasons for each assignment and for every rejected alternative.
.TP
.I prerequisite_warnings.csv
Written only when prerequisite rules were supplied:
student_id, code, course_id, prereq_course_id, message.
An empty file (header only) means the check ran and found nothing.
.SH WARNING CODES
.TP
.B MISSING_PREREQUISITE
A ranked course lists a prerequisite the student has not completed.
.TP
.B NO_COMPLETION_RECORD
The student ranked courses that have prerequisites but has no completion rows.
.I course_id
lists those courses separated by |.
.TP
.B SELF_PREREQUISITE
A rule lists a course as its own prerequisite; the rule is ignored.
.PP
The preference portal uses the same codes and messages. The shared golden file
.I data/prerequisite\-warnings/expected_warnings.csv
is checked by both test suites.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A slotbook was found and exported. Prerequisite warnings do not change this.
.TP
.B 1
The input failed validation, or no complete slotbook was produced (the reasons are printed as
diagnostics).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown option, missing or bad value, missing file), unreadable CSV, or an
unexpected runtime error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Solve the main fixture with UniTime:
.PP
.RS
mvn exec:java \-Dexec.args="\-\-input data/feasible \-\-output output/demo"
.RE
.PP
Use the exact CP\-SAT solver with a 30\-second limit:
.PP
.RS
mvn exec:java \-Dexec.args="\-\-input data/feasible \-\-solver cpsat \-\-time\-limit 30"
.RE
.PP
Solve and report prerequisite warnings (22 warnings, same slotbook as data/feasible):
.PP
.RS
mvn exec:java \-Dexec.args="\-\-input data/prerequisite\-warnings \-\-output output/prereq"
.RE
.PP
Use files downloaded from the portal's admin page:
.PP
.RS
mvn exec:java \-Dexec.args="\-\-input data/feasible \-\-prerequisites ~/Downloads/prerequisites.csv \-\-completed\-courses ~/Downloads/completed_courses.csv"
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
UniTime is a heuristic: on the generated test scenarios it matched CP\-SAT's proven optimum
in 10 of 13 cases. Student and instructor data in the repository are synthetic. Grade cards
uploaded through the portal are self\-reported and unverified. The JavaFX interface exports
.I prerequisite_warnings.csv
but does not yet display warnings on screen.
